  "description": "Joo Seo-Ah and Nam Do-Hyeon have been inseparable friends since middle school, sharing a bond that always felt like equal ground. However, following the implementation of the new age unification law, a technicality shifts their dynamic: Do-Hyeon is officially younger than Seo-Ah. Heartbroken by a recent breakup and nursing a specific craving for the comfort of a firm, youthful younger man to spite her ex, Seo-Ah decides to exploit this sudden age gap. She turns to Do-Hyeon, whose birthday falls just months after hers, and issues a playful yet daring challenge. \n\n\"Hey, Nam Do-Hyeon. Call me Noona,\" she demands. To her surprise, Do-Hyeon actually stammers it out, looking flustered and endearingly shy. Seeing him blush makes Seo-Ah’s heart skip a beat; she suddenly finds him dangerously cute. Panicked, she realizes she’s crossing a line she can't uncross. If he starts looking this adorable, she’s in serious trouble. What on earth is she supposed to do now?\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
